class_name AbilityHooks
extends RefCounted
## AbilityHooks — what abilities do, keyed by OUR hook names. The ROM only stores a numeric ability id per
## species; res://profiles/quetzal_a9v1_battle.json "abilities" maps those ids to our hook keys (generated by
## tools/gen_battle_profile.py from the ROM's own ability names, so only ids + our keys are stored).
## Behaviour follows public mechanics descriptions, with Pokémon Showdown (MIT) as the numeric reference
## (Gen 9 rules, which is what pokeemerald-expansion's GEN_LATEST config follows). Our own code.
##
## Multipliers are 4096-based integers (4915 = x1.2, 5325 = x1.3, 6144 = x1.5, 8192 = x2, 2048 = x0.5,
## 3072 = x0.75), the same fixed-point numbers the games use, so DamageCalc can chain them exactly
## (DamageCalc.chain_all). *_mods() functions return Arrays of those integers.
##
## Hook keys (params in braces). Damage: pinch_boost{type}, double_atk, guts, hustle, resist_types{types},
## marvel_scale, technician, sheer_force, adaptability, tinted_lens, sniper, filter, flag_boost{flag,m},
## punk_rock, reckless, ate{type}, normalize, sand_force, analytic, rivalry, solar_power, dry_skin, heatproof,
## fur_coat, fluffy, ice_scales, multiscale, water_bubble, type_atk{type}, defeatist, flare_boost,
## toxic_boost, paradox{w|t}, neuroforce, friend_guard, unaware, scrappy, merciless.
## Immunities/absorbs: type_immune{type}, absorb_heal{type}, absorb_boost{type}, absorb_stat{type,st,n},
## wonder_guard, flag_immune{flag}, telepathy, damp, oblivious, overcoat, block_priority, status_immune{s},
## leaf_guard, water_bubble, sturdy, disguise, magic_guard, sticky_hold, suction_cups, wonder_skin,
## magic_bounce.
## Stats: no_acc_drop, no_atk_drop, no_def_drop, no_stat_drop, contrary, simple, defiant{st}, moxie{st},
## beast_boost, justified, rattled, stamina, weak_armor, anger_point, steadfast, berserk, entry_boost{st},
## download, speed_boost, moody.
## Status/contact: contact_status{s,pct}, contact_chip{den}, contact_drop{st}, effect_spore, poison_touch,
## cute_charm, cursed_body, aftermath, synchronize, corrosion, poison_heal, shed_skin, hydration,
## natural_cure, regenerator, early_bird.
## Field/entry: entry_drop_foe{st}, entry_weather{w}, entry_terrain{t}, cloud_nine, trace, frisk, trap{type?,
## grounded?}, run_away, pressure, unnerve, gluttony, unburden, klutz, infiltrator, mold_breaker.
## Speed/order: weather_speed{w}, terrain_speed{t}, quick_feet, prankster, gale_wings, triage, stall, truant.
## Misc: no_flinch, no_secondary, no_confuse, no_recoil, acc_mult{num,den}, weather_evasion{w}, no_crit,
## crit_up, no_guard, skill_link, weather_heal{w}, protean, serene_grace.
## Gen 3 parity (0.1.65) and later-gen additions, keyed by ROM ability NAME in FALLBACK_BY_NAME below
## (the profile only maps 200 of the ROM's 319 ability ids; the other 119 are looked up here by name, so
## no ROM ids are hardcoded): plus_minus, forecast, color_change, slow_start, stakeout, grass_pelt,
## water_compaction, sand_spit, seed_sower, steam_engine, anger_shell, anticipation, forewarn, healer,
## bad_dreams, pickpocket, magician, mummy, lingering_aroma, cotton_down, mirror_armor, screen_cleaner,
## supersweet_syrup, curious_medicine, hospitality, perish_body, quick_draw, long_reach, unseen_fist,
## propeller_tail, stalwart, wind_rider, wind_power, electromorphosis, harvest, cheek_pouch, symbiosis,
## power_spot, battery, steely_spirit, victory_star, aura{type}, aura_break, ruin{st}, orichalcum_pulse,
## hadron_engine, supreme_overlord, costar, opportunist, soul_heart, power_of_alchemy, receiver,
## innards_out, toxic_chain, toxic_debris, wimp_out, gorilla_tactics, guard_dog, flower_veil, flower_gift,
## good_as_gold, neutralizing_gas, ice_face, mimicry, mycelium_might.
## Keys with no effect here ("none", and anything unknown) do nothing.
## Every function takes the BattleState `st` first (untyped to avoid a class cycle).
## Depends on: BattleData, BattleMon, TypeChart. Used by: DamageCalc, BattleRules, MoveEffects, BattleState,
## ItemHooks, BattleAI.

## Abilities a Mold Breaker-style attacker ignores on its target (Showdown "breakable" flag; our keys).
const BREAKABLE := ["type_immune", "absorb_heal", "absorb_boost", "absorb_stat", "wonder_guard", "flag_immune",
	"sturdy", "disguise", "multiscale", "filter", "fur_coat", "fluffy", "ice_scales", "resist_types", "marvel_scale",
	"heatproof", "dry_skin", "water_bubble", "unaware", "damp", "oblivious", "overcoat", "no_acc_drop", "no_atk_drop",
	"no_def_drop", "no_stat_drop", "contrary", "simple", "status_immune", "leaf_guard", "no_flinch", "no_confuse",
	"weather_evasion", "no_crit", "sticky_hold", "suction_cups", "wonder_skin", "magic_bounce", "friend_guard",
	"telepathy", "block_priority", "punk_rock", "aroma_veil", "no_secondary"]

